  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Knee osteoarthritis grading by ResNet18 learning\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "***Hi there*, in this project, I fine-tune a pretrained ResNet18 to grade knee articular cartilage, aka knee osteoarthritis, from X-ray images, using the Kellgren-Lawrence (KL) grading system — the clinical standard for classifying these symptoms with the following scale:**\n",
        "#\n",
        "#\n",
        "- - Grade 0 — Healthy knee\n",
        "- - Grade 1 — Doubtful narrowing, possible osteophytic lipping\n",
        "- - Grade 2 — Definite osteophytes, possible joint space narrowing\n",
        "- - Grade 3 — Multiple osteophytes, definite narrowing, mild sclerosis\n",
        "- - Grade 4 — Large osteophytes, severe narrowing, severe sclerosis\n",
        "\n",
        "**Goal would be to take any X-ray from a patient as input and predict its grade, using this machine learning model.**\n",
        "\n",
        "**This dataset - from [kaggle](https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/shashwatwork/knee-osteoarthritis-dataset-with-severity) contains 8260 frontal X-ray of knees, already divided by grade from 0-4 and splitted in test/train/val. images are poorly reparted and it's the main issue we face ub this model. grade 4 is underrepresented when grade 0 and 2 take over 50% of the file.**\n",
       
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "0QkCF2e_np-K"
      },
      "id": "0QkCF2e_np-K"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "ijn6WayipuOn"
      },
